ruan: Metal clients (posters, widgets, apps) run Turnip without the Mesa disk cache

The rbu125u CollectionsPoster report: RUNNINGBOARD 0xDEAD10CC (suspended while holding a file lock), thread in flock inside
libvulkan_freedreno = Mesa's multi-file disk cache writer (src/util/disk_cache_os.c:807, flock LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB on the
temporary cache file while it writes). backboardd, the render server, keeps the cache; every other process gets
MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true (src/util/disk_cache_os.c:1033 disk_cache_enabled) before clientDevice() loads Turnip.
overwrite=0: a value already in the environment wins. Apply from UniXNU/drivers/AdrenoMetal with patch -p1.

--- a/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
+++ b/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
@@ -458,7 +458,13 @@
             return device;
         }
 #else
-        if (!nativeIsRenderServer()) return device = clientDevice(port);
+        if (!nativeIsRenderServer()) {
+            // ruan: no Mesa disk cache outside the render server. Its writer takes flock on cache files (util/disk_cache_os.c:807), and
+            // a poster suspended by RunningBoard while holding it is killed 0xDEAD10CC (rbu125u CollectionsPoster, thread in flock in
+            // libvulkan_freedreno). Set before clientDevice loads Turnip, whose tu_physical_device_init reads it in disk_cache_create.
+            setenv("MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE", "true", 0);
+            return device = clientDevice(port);
+        }
 #endif
         // The discovery releases the accelerator port when it is done; the monitor and the scanout client keep using it.
         if (void *iokit = dlopen("/System/Library/Frameworks/IOKit.framework/IOKit", RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL)) {
